%description:
Tests SO_RCVBUF on an open connection (TcpSocket::setReceiveBufferSize()), which
locks the receive buffer, as Linux SOCK_RCVBUF_LOCK. The scenario is that of
tcp_rcvbuf_grow_1, but the server application sets the buffer to 8000 bytes on
its open socket at t=0.8 s. A locked buffer offers only its free space at the
truesize ratio of the received segments (112/256): 8000 bytes give 3500. The
right edge of the handshake offer (8001) does not move back, so the offers go
down from 7000 to 3500 as RCV.NXT moves toward that edge. windowAutoTuning does
not grow a locked buffer: STATUS reports skRcvbuf=8000 at t=3 s, where
tcp_rcvbuf_grow_1 grows it to 18240.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 10s
*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 20000"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1000
*.*_tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.*_tcp.sackSupport = true
*.srv_tcp.advertisedWindow = 8000
*.srv_tcp.receiveBufferSize = 8000B
*.srv_tcp.windowAutoTuning = true
*.srv_app.rcvBufScript="0.8 8000"
*.srv_app.statusRequestScript="0.5,3"
*.tcptester.script="a12 delete"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.003 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 1001 win 7000 
[1.005 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1001:2001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.005 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A 2001:3001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.007 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 2001 win 6000 
[1.007 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 3001 win 5000 
[1.009 A006] A.1000 > B.2000: A 3001:4001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.009 A007] A.1000 > B.2000: A 4001:5001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.009 A008] A.1000 > B.2000: A 5001:6001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.009 A009] A.1000 > B.2000: A 6001:7001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.011 B005] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 4001 win 4000 
[1.011 B006] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 5001 win 3500 
[1.011 B007] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 6001 win 3500 
[1.011 B008] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 7001 win 3500 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
SO_RCVBUF: the receive buffer is 8000 bytes, locked
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%not-contains: stdout
STATUS: skRcvbuf=18240
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
